<title>USA: San Jose, Calif., mayor proposes revenue bonds.</title>
<headline>San Jose, Calif., mayor proposes revenue bonds.</headline>
<dateline>SAN JOSE, Calif. 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>San Jose Mayor Susan Hammer has proposed issuing $6 to $10 million of revenue bonds to aid child care providers in the city.</p>
<p>Under the plan, the city would issue the bonds to buy portable buildings. The buildings would then be leased to child care providers in order to pay off the bonds, Hammer spokesman Kevin Pursglove said Tuesday.</p>
<p>Hammer will provide more details about the revenue bond plan later this week, her spokesman said.</p>
